## Project Overview
This project is an end-to-end machine learning application for estimating NYC taxi fares.

## Original Prompt
<professor/coding-agent prompt>

## Dataset
Kaggle-compatible NYC taxi data / simulated NYC-like records.

## What the Project Does
Users select:
- Pickup location
- Drop-off location
- Number of passengers
- Pickup hour

The application estimates the taxi fare and displays an uncertainty range.

## Machine Learning Model
The deployed model is a Ridge Regression model.

## Main Features
- Interactive trip estimator
- Pickup/drop-off map
- Fare prediction
- Uncertainty range
- Model monitoring
- Feature importance
- CRISP-DM workflow

## CRISP-DM Process

### 1. Business Understanding
Estimate the taxi fare before pickup.

### 2. Data Understanding
Analyze trip coordinates, time, passenger count, and fare.

### 3. Data Preparation
Clean invalid values and create useful features such as trip distance.

### 4. Modeling
Compare multiple regression approaches and select the best-performing model.

### 5. Evaluation
Evaluate the model using RMSE, MAE, and explained variance.

### 6. Deployment
Expose the trained model through the interactive web application.

## Model Performance
- Test RMSE: approximately $2.07
- MAE: approximately $1.63
- Explained variance: approximately 98.8%
- Prediction coverage: 91%

## Model Explainability
Trip distance has the largest impact on the predicted fare.

